@page {
    route: "/all-syntax/",
    draft: False,
    theme: "paper",
    color_scheme: "auto",
    meta: {
        title: "All syntax",
        description: "Rocdown kitchen sink",
    },
}

@roc {
Status : [Ready, Loading]

items = [{ name: "alpha" }, { name: "beta" }]
status = Ready
show_notice = True
published = "2026-08-23"
}

@context { ready : Bool }

@init {
    { ready: True }
}

@css {
    body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; }
}

@component
Hello = |{ name ?? "World" }| {
    @css {
        p { color: inherit; }
    }
    <p>Hello, {name}</p>
}

@fixture{target: Hello}
helloSample = { name: "Roc" }

@post:fragment("/actions/all-syntax/ping") = |_| {
    hello({ name: "pong" })
}

# All syntax

Published @{published}. Use \@{upstream} or `@{upstream}` in a code span.

Email docs@example.com or mention @roclang. Visit https://example.com or see
[[syntax-v2]], [v2](syntax-v2.rocdown), and [the heading](#explicit-heading).

This is **bold**, *italic*, ~~struck~~, and `inline code`.

- list item
- [x] done
- [ ] todo

1. ordered item

> A quotation.

---

![A banana](./img/yammi_banana.png)

See [ref text][blocks].

[blocks]: syntax-v2.rocdown

```roc
answer = 42
```

| col | val |
| --- | --- |
| a | b |

@render Hello({ name: "render" })

<Hello name="island" />

@let visible = List.keep_if(items, |_| True)

@if show_notice {
    <p>Notice</p>
} @else if List.is_empty(visible) {
    <p>Empty</p>
} @else {
    <ul>
        @for item in visible {
            <li>{item.name}</li>
        }
    </ul>
}

@for item in visible {
    <li>{item.name}</li>
}

@match status {
    Loading => <p>Loading</p>
    Ready => <Hello name="ready" />
}

:h2[id: "explicit-heading"] Explicit heading

:figure[caption: "A banana", credit: "Rocci fixtures"] {{
    :img[src: "./img/yammi_banana.png", alt: "A banana", width: "50px"]
}}

:img[src: "./img/yammi_banana.png", decorative: True, width: "20px"]

:note Don't do this.

:tip Line-scope still works.

:caution[title: "Watch"] Prefer `:caution` over leftover `@docs`.

:danger Do not paste raw HTML.

:deprecated This spelling is kept for coverage.

:note[title: "Watch"] {{
Nested section body.
}}

:details[summary: "More", open: False] Nested details body.

:definition[term: "Article block"] A `:kind[params]` node with a body.

:badge[label: "preview", tone: "preview"]

:steps.begin
    :step[title: "One"] First step.
    :step[title: "Two", verify: True] Second step.
:steps.end

:tabs.begin[group: "os", kind: "platform"]
    :tab[id: "mac", label: "macOS"] Mac panel.
    :tab[id: "linux", label: "Linux"] Linux panel.
:tabs.end

:tabs[group: "install", kind: "tool"] {{
    :tab[id: "cli", label: "CLI"] Check the catalog.
    :tab[id: "test", label: "Examples"] Run declared examples.
}}

:card-grid.begin
    :link-card[href: "https://example.com", title: "Example", summary: "External page"]
    :link-card[href: "https://roc-lang.org", title: "Roc"]
:card-grid.end

:file-tree {{
- test/
    - AllSyntax.rocdown
    - snippet.txt
}}

:compatibility[caption: "Hosts"] {{
| Host | Status |
| --- | --- |
| Native | yes |
}}

:include[path: "snippet.txt", language: "text"]

:example[language: "sh", test: ["/bin/echo", "hello"], expect: "hello"] {{
```sh
echo hello
```
}}

\@if this is escaped

More markdown after.[^note]

[^note]: Footnotes stay in ordinary Rocdown and include a backlink.
